{"id": "EUVD-2026-82135", "enisaUuid": "7e03f11c-32d0-3589-9c6e-27c901e5453e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/erdma: Fix CEQ tasklet use-after-free on removal\n\nEach CEQ interrupt handler only schedules eqc->tasklet. The tasklet calls\nerdma_ceq_completion_handler(), which reads the DMA-coherent EQ ring\nthrough get_next_valid_eqe() and updates eq->dbrec through notify_eq().\n\nerdma_ceqs_uninit() frees each CEQ IRQ and then destroys its EQ.\nfree_irq() prevents another hard IRQ and waits for an in-flight handler,\nbut it does not drain a tasklet that the handler already scheduled. The\ntasklet can therefore access eq->qbuf or eq->dbrec after\nerdma_eq_destroy() frees them.\n\nClearing ceq_cb->ready does not synchronize with a tasklet that already\npassed the check at the start of erdma_ceq_completion_handler().\n\nKill the tasklet after free_irq(), when no handler can schedule it again,\nand before erdma_ceq_uninit_one() releases the EQ buffers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e8b78dabb1f156db05ffe74c6eae861167c7c21", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e129c1310abfa786a510cc63e69c5ef12349048", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f738c0a372d36a10dfae6dc357717c13b2aa72f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a60c36d8d17f1b86705523d5eb6d290df28831e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61a25b8d333e1eb2a189881d516f8d5194e26840", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ca79979384f031d710c4b3bae065dcb5d95aca3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mcv5-xwww-xj32", "CVE-2026-92514"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "29b4157c-2064-3980-9c99-11ca87705edc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2e2ce597-a7b0-33a8-93fe-fff56fa428ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <6e129c1310abfa786a510cc63e69c5ef12349048"}, {"id": "33520d52-0038-3a4c-929b-7a62f75d6054", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "44288bbd-5a76-3738-a1e3-5ff3bf708565", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "4bfd4ab6-94e4-3253-9d36-6bc975f4bfe5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <61a25b8d333e1eb2a189881d516f8d5194e26840"}, {"id": "5877c4f4-83d2-3749-9cb4-5406c26f009a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <0e8b78dabb1f156db05ffe74c6eae861167c7c21"}, {"id": "86c719ec-8669-386f-a89b-a65c147fd795", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "9f24cf17-82cc-3366-86b7-2c79a20f104e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "ab3f58d9-c25e-32ba-b4c5-90a2f2ec9a9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <a60c36d8d17f1b86705523d5eb6d290df28831e5"}, {"id": "bb21c899-0ea6-3e30-a63d-616c4adc98ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <f738c0a372d36a10dfae6dc357717c13b2aa72f4"}, {"id": "cfa18067-c065-301a-a2cd-84e9c1d3fc43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "e951e8f3-61c6-3f74-8fb8-7b230dbe522c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a0a630b953451a59a2612ad8c29246638f0a38 <0ca79979384f031d710c4b3bae065dcb5d95aca3"}, {"id": "f2f86d14-3d6d-38f1-bce4-e1c8c1d97906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "fd39f52c-8c90-3fff-84e0-556ae0e